1.)Pick any one feature from a popular app you use daily (for example: Instagram signup, Flipkart add-to-cart, or Paytm recharge) and write 5 clear requirements for that feature.
Answers :
-Feature: Flipkart – Add to Cart
-Product Selection: The user should be able to select a product and add it to the shopping cart.
-Cart Update: After adding a product, the cart should immediately display the selected product, quantity, price, and total amount.
-Quantity Management: The user should be able to increase or decrease the quantity of a product in the cart.
-Stock Validation: The system should prevent users from adding a product to the cart if it is out of stock.
-Cart Persistence: Products added to the cart should remain saved when the user navigates to other



2.)For the requirements you wrote in Task 1, create a table mapping each requirement to at least one test case that would verify it works as intended.<br><br><em><strong>Hint:</strong> Your table should have columns: Requirement ID, Requirement Description, Test Case ID, Test Case Description.</em>
Answer :
Requirement 1: User should be able to select a product and add it to the cart.
Test Case 1: Select an available product and click Add to Cart. Verify that the product is successfully added to the cart.

Requirement 2: The cart should display the product, quantity, price, and total amount.
Test Case 2: Open the cart after adding a product. Verify that the product name, quantity, price, and total amount are displayed correctly.

Requirement 3: User should be able to increase or decrease the product quantity.
Test Case 3: Increase and decrease the product quantity in the cart. Verify that the quantity and total price are updated correctly.

Requirement 4: The system should prevent users from adding an out-of-stock product to the cart.
Test Case 4: Select an out-of-stock product and try to add it to the cart. Verify that the product is not added and an appropriate message is displayed.

Requirement 5: Products should remain in the cart when the user navigates to other pages.
Test Case 5: Add a product to the cart, navigate to another page, and return to the cart. Verify that the product is still present.



