4.)Explain in 3-4 sentences the difference between forward traceability and backward traceability in the context of your table. Give one example of each using your requirements and test cases.
Answer :
1.)Forward traceability means checking that every requirement is linked to one or more test cases to make sure all requirements are tested.
-For example, the requirement “User should be able to sign up” is linked to Test Case TC01.
2.)Backward traceability means starting from a test case and checking which requirement it was created to test.
-For example, Test Case TC02, which checks whether the user receives an OTP, can be traced backward to the requirement “User should receive OTP.” This helps ensure that no unnecessary test cases exist and every test case has a valid requirement.




5.)Create a bi-directional RTM (Requirements Traceability Matrix) for the login feature of a food delivery app like Zomato, showing how each requirement is linked to test cases and how test cases trace back to requirements.<br><br><em><strong>Constraint:</strong> Include at least 3 requirements and 5 test cases in your matrix.</em>
Answer :
Requirements
R1: User should be able to log in with valid mobile number and password.
R2: User should see an error message when incorrect login credentials are entered.
R3: User should be able to log in using OTP.
R4: User should be able to use the “Forgot Password” option.

Bi-Directional RTM
R1 – Valid Login
Requirement → Test Cases: TC01, TC02
TC01 → Verify login with valid mobile number and password.
TC02 → Verify login with valid credentials after entering all required fields.

R2 – Invalid Login
Requirement → Test Cases: TC03
TC03 → Verify that an error message is displayed for an incorrect password.

R3 – OTP Login
Requirement → Test Cases: TC04
TC04 → Verify that the user can log in successfully using a valid OTP.

R4 – Forgot Password
Requirement → Test Cases: TC05
TC05 → Verify that the user can reset the password using the “Forgot Password” option.
Backward Traceability
TC01 → R1: Valid login test traces back to the valid login requirement.
TC02 → R1: Required-field/login validation test traces back to R1.
TC03 → R2: Invalid credentials test traces back to the error-handling requirement.
TC04 → R3: OTP login test traces back to the OTP login requirement.
TC05 → R4: Forgot password test traces back to the password recovery requirement.
